2026-04-14T23:31:42.2498620Z pybind11 provides CMake targets. There are two modes provided; classic, which is built on the old Python
2026-04-14T23:31:42.2500140Z discovery packages in CMake, or the new FindPython mode, which uses FindPython
2026-04-14T23:31:42.2501700Z from 3.12+ forward (3.15+ _highly_ recommended).
2026-04-14T23:31:42.2502120Z 
2026-04-14T23:31:42.2502330Z New FindPython mode:
2026-04-14T23:31:42.2502600Z 
2026-04-14T23:31:42.2503040Z     find_package(Python COMPONENTS Interpreter Development)
2026-04-14T23:31:42.2503790Z     find_package(pybind11 CONFIG)
2026-04-14T23:31:42.2504120Z 
2026-04-14T23:31:42.2504300Z     # pybind11 method:
2026-04-14T23:31:42.2504850Z     pybind11_add_module(MyModule1 src1.cpp)
2026-04-14T23:31:42.2505230Z 
2026-04-14T23:31:42.2505390Z     # Python method:
2026-04-14T23:31:42.2505920Z     Python_add_library(MyModule2 src2.cpp)
2026-04-14T23:31:42.2506700Z     target_link_libraries(MyModule2 pybind11::headers)
2026-04-14T23:31:42.2507480Z     set_target_properties(MyModule2 PROPERTIES
2026-04-14T23:31:42.2508170Z         INTERPROCEDURAL_OPTIMIZATION ON
2026-04-14T23:31:42.2508790Z         CXX_VISIBILITY_PRESET ON
2026-04-14T23:31:42.2509390Z         VISIBILITY_INLINES_HIDDEN ON
2026-04-14T23:31:42.2509880Z     )
2026-04-14T23:31:42.2510070Z 
2026-04-14T23:31:42.2510380Z For more information see here:
2026-04-14T23:31:42.2511300Z     https://pybind11.readthedocs.io/en/latest/compiling.html#building-with-cmake
